amentals point clearly one way (post-redistricting), so it is treated as safe for that party."]}, "overview": "Utah's newly drawn 1st District favors Democrats after redistricting, and Ben McAdams enters the general election with every structural advantage. He has raised $2.3 million and benefits from $2.7 million in outside support, while Republican Riley Owen has raised about $133,000 with minimal cash on hand. A September poll of likely voters showed McAdams leading by more than 40 points, and prediction markets put his win probability at 96 to 97 percent.\n\nDebate coverage from late September and October shows the two candidates finding common ground on costs and AI policy, but no evidence has emerged that the race is competitive. The forecast treats this as a Safe Democratic hold with a margin in the mid-20s, with uncertainty reflecting the thin polling record rather than any sign of a real contest.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9908, "margin": 20.9}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.99, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9893, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9909, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9895, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9899, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9906, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9886, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9895, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9907, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.99, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9979, "margin": 28.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9958, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.997, "margin": 27.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9991, "margin": 28.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9988, "margin": 27.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9979, "margin": 27.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9971, "margin": 27.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9972, "margi